 section's replace holds at 2, 4 and 8 vCPUs, and a followed file lost 308 to
 614 accesses a run on windows-2025 until its change was counted under the
 lock

The record, D189's sentence, and a storm that makes fewer replaces where its threads outnumber the host's cores: a paced replace took about 24 ms there against 0.26 ms, 481 to 525 s a run. slates' diag-shards-whp-4, run 41981896876.

